{"3224480": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Light the Candles in Hell", "steam_appid": 3224480, "required_age": 0, "is_free": true, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Disclaimer: This game is a simple walking simulator with only one interaction. I aimed to create a meditative experience inspired by Camino de Santiago pilgrimage in Spain, but it didn’t turn out as planned. Reviews are negative, with players feeling it's a bit of a time waster, instead of taking it down from Steam, I’ve left it up. This was my first game, made in just three days, and it’s far from optimized. I wouldn’t necessarily recommend playing it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Playtime: 2 minutes</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You light the 11 candles. There is no sound, no one around. In the vast open world, a single monolith stands, marking your time in hell. The sole purpose is to keep the flame alive.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game offers very simple gameplay. Players light 11 candles one by one and aim to light them all.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When all candles are lit, the ending appears and the game is complete.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Disclaimer: This game is a simple walking simulator with only one interaction. I aimed to create a meditative experience inspired by Camino de Santiago pilgrimage in Spain, but it didn’t turn out as planned. Reviews are negative, with players feeling it's a bit of a time waster, instead of taking it down from Steam, I’ve left it up. This was my first game, made in just three days, and it’s far from optimized. I wouldn’t necessarily recommend playing it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Playtime: 2 minutes</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You light the 11 candles. There is no sound, no one around. In the vast open world, a single monolith stands, marking your time in hell. The sole purpose is to keep the flame alive.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game offers very simple gameplay. Players light 11 candles one by one and aim to light them all.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When all candles are lit, the ending appears and the game is complete.</p>", "short_description": "Light the candles in hell, a journey for those you hold dear.", "supported_languages": "English", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3224480/header.jpg?t=1779206618", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3224480/aa260a5346e01a1d899c781590ebfe769697e6e4/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1779206618", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3224480/aa260a5346e01a1d899c781590ebfe769697e6e4/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1779206618", "website": null, "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10 or later (64-bit)<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> i5-3570 3.4 Ghz 4 Core<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 16 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Nvidia GTX 1650/GTX 1050-ti, or AMD RX 470/RX570, or equivalent performance &amp; VRAM<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 11<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 2 GB available space<br></li><li><strong>Sound Card:</strong> realtek</li></ul>", "recommended": "<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>